; The Familiar: a creature of the wizard's own light that keeps by him and fights what comes close
; (scripts/Familiar.cs). It is taken in one of three FORMS - a dog, a crow or a cat - chosen on the page
; that follows its card the first time it is taken, and the form holds for the run (SpellData.Variants,
; .ai/decisions/2026-10-28-spell-variants.md). Eric, 2026-10-28: "crow moves faster, cat gives passive
; bonuses, dog does the most direct damage. they each have their own mutations/ascensions".
;
; Everything a form decides is in its sub-resource below: its name, icon, words, numbers and level table
; replace the spell's when it is chosen (SpellVariants.Apply), and its milestones are its own
; (SpellEvolutionCatalog.SetupFamiliarEvolutions). The numbers at the foot of this file are only the
; template's - the dog's, the default - which no run plays. A form never changes the tags: every one is
; pure Arcane.
;
; BaseDamage is ONE STRIKE (a bite, a peck, a swipe) on the quarry and anything else inside its reach
; (the jaws, the beak, the claws - Familiar's own radii, times the player's Area and every milestone's
; AreaMultiplier). BaseCooldown is the strike rate: every cooldown hands each creature one strike, which
; it spends the moment its quarry is in reach. BaseRange is how far from the wizard it hunts. Amount adds
; no creature - each is a whole second attacker (Player.FireFamiliar). Every form catches enemy bolts
; aimed at him, in its own way (Familiar, "Catching bolts").
;
; Every table is written out in full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own (every
; level has a damage line, every even level a cooldown line, and no form's tags carry ProjectileCount),
; and no line names a size in pixels.

; --- THE DOG: the hound pack the Familiar was before it had forms - the most direct damage. It goes for
; whatever nears the wizard, leaps and bites. One hound; the second joins at level 3 (2026-10-28, Eric:
; "you should only start with one familiar, getting 2 of them should be an upgrade"). Every level adds 4
; to the bite, even levels take the cooldown step, odd levels widen the hunt by 20 (and the leap with
; it). Level 8: 44 a bite every 0.68 s from two hounds.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_dog_2"]
script = ExtResource("2")
Level = 2
DamageBonus = 4
CooldownBonus = -0.08

